<h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
<p class="emst-lede">The explorer aims to conform to WCAG 2.2 Level AA, which covers Section 508 (WCAG 2.0 AA) and the ADA Title II rule (WCAG 2.1 AA).</p>
<ul class="usa-list">
  <li>Every chart has a heading that states its message, a text summary and a data table. No information is shown by color alone or only on hover.</li>
  <li>All disclosures are native HTML and work with a keyboard and without JavaScript. The gap-check rating controls are ordinary radio buttons with targets of at least 24 by 24 pixels.</li>
  <li>Pages reflow to 320 CSS pixels wide; wide tables scroll inside their own box.</li>
  <li>Automated checks (axe-core, WCAG 2.0 to 2.2 A and AA rules) and a manual keyboard and screen-reader checklist run before each release. The current accessibility conformance report is in the <a href="{{ '/download/' | url }}">downloads</a> and in the repository at <code>site/ACR.md</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Known limits are listed in the conformance report. To report a barrier, use the <a href="{{ '/challenge/' | url }}">challenge route</a> and say which page and what assistive technology you use.</p>
